# Build context filter for docker_build(..., ".") in the Tiltfile — every
# beat (rattle, clank, hiss, thump, bootstrap) builds from this same repo
# root context, so anything left un-ignored here gets tarred, hashed, and
# shipped to BuildKit five times over. No .dockerignore existed before this
# (2026-07-31 investigation): the build context was the full ~14GB repo dir,
# dominated by .otelc-build/gocache's 12GB local Go build cache.

# otelc's generated instrumentation/pkg trees (go.mod replace targets, see
# Dockerfile's `COPY .otelc-build ./.otelc-build`) ARE needed and must stay
# out of this ignore list — mirrors .gitignore's same carve-out. Only the
# scratch/cache byproducts of running the otelc tool locally are ignored.
.otelc-build/gocache/
.otelc-build/debug/
.otelc-build/debug.log
.otelc-build/build-plan.log
.otelc-build/matched.json
.otelc-build/added_imports.*.json

# Build output — never an input to the image build
bin/
dist/
*.test
coverage.*

# VCS metadata — not needed inside the build
.git/

# Secrets — never belongs in a build context
.env
.env.*

# Editor/OS/Agent cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.zed/
.claude/
.gemini/
.agents/
Tiltfile.tmp.*
.otelc-build/state*


# Neither a build input nor stable during a live session — testdata fixtures
# get appended to by running tests/harnesses, and *.md notes get edited
# live, and docker_build(..., ".") has no other filter watching this whole
# tree. Each write was retriggering a full five-image rebuild + redeploy,
# visible as thump-bootstrap (a Job, so it gets deleted/recreated each time)
# looping continuously. Found live, 2026-08-03.
**/testdata/**
*.md
